articles.content_en:
Article 24 Residents of the Macao Special Administrative Region, referred to as Macao residents, shall include permanent residents and non-permanent residents. Permanent residents of the Macao Special Administrative Region shall be:
(1) Chinese citizens born in Macao before or after the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region and their children of Chinese nationality born outside Macao;
(2) Chinese citizens who have ordinarily resided in Macao for a continuous period of not less than seven years before or after the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region and their children of Chinese nationality born outside Macao after they have become permanent residents;
(3) Portuguese who were born in Macao before or after the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region and who have taken Macao as their permanent place of residence;
(4) Portuguese who have ordinarily resided in Macao for a continuous period of not less than seven years before or after the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region and who have taken Macao as their permanent place of residence;
(5) Other persons who have ordinarily resided in Macao for a continuous period of not less than seven years before or after the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region and who have taken Macao as their permanent place of residence;
(6) Children under the age of 18 born in Macao before or after the establishment of the Macao Special Administrative Region of the permanent residents referred to in item (5). The above-mentioned residents shall have the right of abode in the Macao Special Administrative Region and shall be eligible for permanent identity cards of the Macao Special Administrative Region. Non-permanent residents of the Macao Special Administrative Region shall be persons who are eligible for identity cards of the Macao Special Administrative Region in accordance with the laws of the Macao Special Administrative Region but who have no right of abode.
